	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "2x12 2.54 mm stacking SOCKET, on the driver board's front. Pin 1 square and at 185 V; position 4 HAS NO HOLE - it is the key, snipped on the header and plugged on the socket, and the silkscreen ring marks it. Odd pins in one column, even in the other, rows stepping along y (KiCad PinHeader_2x12_P2.54mm_Vertical numbering). Pre-rotated 270 deg counter-clockwise (front view), per this repo's no-rotation-token convention.")
